wciVwepCWEceZJH9BvoftDoBZKn_FeJrxYWVj0-8rCsPWn7JwUCoeMl2_AxjJ_yPPYm7u2RXGek8pSoQRxdN9wIhZzcGX2BLSv3sLW8gY6x9CH9v7y-XH3nmDJxUixOGFfjDXY_eV7U8","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Calculating primes and analysis**\n\nI need to compute prime numbers greater than 1000. The list includes 1009, 1013, 1019, 1021, and others up to 1097. Checking for composites and their relationships is essential. I’ve figured out some combinations, like 1037 as itself and 1061 with other factors. I've also looked into one-letter communes in France and considered Bucharest as a fallback since no one-letter city fits. So, I'm analyzing efficient modulo for my findings."},{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Analyzing candidates for residue**\n\nI'm checking residues of candidates modulo 30 to see if they equal 11 or 17. It looks like 1001 gives a residue of 11, and 1007 gives 17, so that works! I also find that 1091 fits as having a residue of 11. So, I've identified some good candidates based on these residues, which could be useful for whatever analysis I'm doing with primes! I want to keep my calculations accurate and consistent."}]},{"id":"rs_036789e885246198016ac278ec41dc819381641e57850c297a","type":"reasoning","content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqwnjvz-9qgFDqknMD3Jp_b_-sr2i-t9Ahwbn-79rffL7UAFHa1Hml-41QVFYt5-5oFz-QW5EbGpb2DuXOiKoWeVxvD6gNsvImcOvcIAGnKVMo8ST1IKJXpgg3cO2kYDMLxrGuzUKJtCEsTzAwzINSeK5QT8BFKGDigd2trCCml-a3MvoXeasTSfo1WMzPFHeMQhqOcAhfQWhY7uET482uBKvSqwbNxgSnl_OvnLUZOBvEgHu2krizDR_vZttmlBmQM7u720IMKVtNx-3hDxRZQDDGg7OYqTZ7byX6_YT6tlwCCQVYku84KNT71XGhasHvdJL0spsGLeh8ikyBjt5s4QsBTYZnYCTrZLytPGaCciGd0jtHBYluEMYNQK4cX6-o6R__Ac3wz8Y2sqJrKRebkJwNuwr0X-e9tYlj7_MApDXeKvr3_aRbVIGu8cD7TQNP8-ojz5jiqMlnfItPbyyLw7jf3QJ687Boog7yOxmcgHh8tB6SiNiKBNw9nYJ75zEnQO_gFARmI7b21YkjVxnXe4RIe1k1tFUEDopfKYjS4ex3ezyqJiTQrmbWjrXEfNybA0AGhmzMk32cksXbpSADFpl7vtZLizHvtwAz7iEJKFOh0Q8Jlz5UcifoN8SCbjE1YsQya2wRtUjWV_VgWTVVwzGOp8bhJm9yfHojp0g4EjN5PfM3LNovr6y6zhGppmu44G5eZN0vSxUW9JUcM42Cql4wA19DLpus-lMmiVt7